## Code Generation Rules for Cursor AI Agent

### Language Requirements
- **NEVER use Korean characters in any code generation**
- **ALL code, comments, variable names, function names, class names, and strings MUST be in English only**
- **ALL documentation and comments MUST be written in English**

### Specific Restrictions
- No Korean characters (한글) in:
  - Variable names
  - Function names
  - Class names
  - Interface names
  - Type names
  - String literals
  - Template literals
  - Comments (single-line // and multi-line /* */)
  - JSDoc comments
  - Console.log messages
  - Error messages
  - Any other text content

### Code Style
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Follow ESLint rules configured in .eslintrc.js
- Use Prettier formatting
- Add final newline to all files
- Use 2 spaces for indentation
- Use single quotes for strings
- Use semicolons

### Examples of FORBIDDEN code:
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG - Korean characters
const 사용자명 = 'John';
function 계산하기() { /* 계산 로직 */ }
console.log('안녕하세요');

// ❌ WRONG - Korean comments
// 이 함수는 사용자 정보를 가져옵니다
function getUserInfo() {
  return user;
}
```

### Examples of CORRECT code:
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT - English only
const userName = 'John';
function calculateTotal() { /* calculation logic */ }
console.log('Hello World');

// ✅ CORRECT - English comments
// This function retrieves user information
function getUserInfo() {
  return user;
}
```

### File Requirements
- All files must end with a newline
- Use UTF-8 encoding
- Use LF line endings
- Follow TypeScript/JavaScript naming conventions

### Error Prevention
- Always check generated code for Korean characters before suggesting
- If Korean input is provided, translate concepts to English equivalents
- Suggest English alternatives for Korean technical terms
